{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1305100-lubberland-a-changeling-campaign-setting","id":1305100,"title":"LUBBERLAND: A Changeling Campaign Setting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-15T12:11:40-07:00","id":1305100,"title":"LUBBERLAND: A Changeling Campaign Setting","content":"Below is a campaign setting I have been tinkering with. It was initially made for an all-childling game centered around Lubberland Academy, in a Harry Potter sort of campaign. But I am so sick of Harry Potter, and I think some more complex stories and mixed Seeming games would work here.<br /> <br /> <b>LUBBERLAND</b><br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/c8/21/0e/c8210ea9ff2a7d974374ae6a80b151b9.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Lubberland is a Fae Realm in the Near Dreaming within the Kingdom of Apples (Northeast United States). This Fae Realm is a one of many mythic America's envisioned by immigrants coming to the \u201cNew World\u201d. It is part of the Big Rock-Candy Mountain mythos that gave rise to the many songs about Hobos Paradise. It\u2019s an old legend akin to the European Cloud Cuckoo Land (where Pinocchio got his Donkey Ears and Tail). It is a wild place, with rolling hills and deep forests.<br /> This realm was founded by the White Pine Covenant during Colonial days between Kithain commoners and several Nunnehi tribes (May-may-gwya-shi and Rock Giants), who remain in the realm today. Though the realm acknowledges the rule of King Peter, they remain stubbornly democratic.<br /> <br /> <b>Features</b><br /> <br /> <b>Big Rock Candy Mountain</b> (Hobo Paradise, Sweet Potato Mountains): A large mountain and center of the realm. The mountain itself is composed of rock hard sugar, though still needing a pickaxe to mine properly. Locals use rock mined from the mountain to brew a range of alcoholic beverages, not least of which is Whiskey. Rock Giants and some Trolls make their homes on the high slopes of the mountain.<br /> <br /> <b>Hobo Jungle: </b>A wild and dangerous forest with only the faintest of trods running through it. Orphan Chimera, Nervosa and other unpleasant types dwell here. The forest straddles the Near and Far Dreaming, and gets wilder the deeper in you go. Secret trods are said to connect from the forest to the Autumn world, from which mortals are sometimes stolen by wicked fae.<br /> <br /> <b>Lubberland Academy: </b>Lubberland Academy is a co-ed boarding school for students in grades 5 through 12 (10-18-year-olds). A school for &quot;gifted youngster&quot; supposedly located in the Catskills. The school is dedicated to teaching Childlings (fae and kinain) how to use their magic and to nurture Fae spirits. The school is a mix of New School and Old Boarding school. Set a bit beyond Scarperton, where most of the school\u2019s staff live.<br /> <br /> <b>Scarperton (Faerie Town):</b> A town in the Near Dreaming, where chimera, kinain, enchanted mortals and changelings live. The town is a mish-mash of architecture, from colonial and native longhouses to more modern dwellings. Built around an ancient railroad trod that winds through the hills and forests, this trod leads back to the Autumn World and into the Deep Dreaming.<br /> <br /> <b>Catskill Railroad: </b>A Trod run mostly by chimera. It is a wild route through the Dreaming, and hosts trains of differing sorts. Some of the tracks pass through the Hobo Jungle. Several locomotives make use of this trod such as The Screaming Jenny; a Nocker built train which serves the needs of Scarperton and others along the track, and the Hellbound Train; run by a Noctnitsu conductor that carries lost souls to nightmare realms.<br /> <br /> <b>AUTUMN WORLD LOCATIONS</b><br /> The Autumn side of Lubberland connects with the area around Shandaken, Woodstock, Kinston and Phoenicia. These small, historic towns and their adjacent wilderness have much to offer the Fae.<br /> <br /> <b>Catskill Mountain Railroad:</b> The Catskill Mountain Railroad (CMRR), is a heritage railroad based in Kingston, New York, that runs a tourist operation through historic routes. A number of industrious fae work here, investing glamour and money into the place.<br /> <br /> <b>Empire State Railroad Museum (Freehold): </b>Established in 1960, the Empire State Railway Museum is a non-profit railroad museum in the historic Ulster &amp; Delaware Phoenicia Railroad Station, Phoenicia, New York. A track from Kingston comes through this museum and runs a tour through the local hill. The Museum is a fully functional rail station in the Near Dreaming, catering to fae and the enchanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 04-18-2019, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T20:43:32-07:00","id":1305630,"title":"","content":"This sounds sweet. The idea of a rail Trod is brilliant, and works with your America/Concordia theme really well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}